  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a list of strings strstrstr. Your task is to find the longest common prefix among all the strings in the list. If there is no common prefix, return −1-1−1.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input:\n\nThe first line contains an integer N, the number of strings.\nThe next line contain a string array str.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the longest common prefix. If there is no common prefix, output −1-1−1.",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= T <= 100",
      "1 <= N <= 100",
      "1 <= length of each string <= 100",
      "All strings consist of lowercase English letters"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "First line contains an integer T, the number of test cases. Each test case consists of two lines: the first line contains an integer N, the number of strings. The second line contains N strings separated by single spaces.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print the longest common prefix of the N strings. If no common prefix exists, print -1. Each answer is printed on its own line.",
    "notes": [],
